    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflectors on both sides to define the entry point, particularly in low-visibility or nighttime conditions.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles so responding units can reach the structure without stopping to reposition.\n• Trim shrubs along the driveway that narrow the travel path or reduce sight lines for approaching vehicles.\n• Keep shrubs adjacent to the structure trimmed back so responders can move around the exterior of the building without obstruction.\n• Identify and maintain a turnaround area near the structure so fire and emergency vehicles can exit without reversing the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep the walkway clear of vegetation overgrowth so responders can move quickly between the driveway and building entry points.\n• Clear dry or dead vegetation from the area immediately surrounding the structure so it does not carry fire toward the building during a wildland or grass fire response."
