    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against or touching the exterior walls of the structure.\n• Thin the trees in the cluster nearest the structure to create open gaps between individual trees.\n• Remove shrubs growing beneath tree canopies near the structure to break up vertical layers of vegetation.\n• Cut or mow grass growing close to the structure down to a short height.\n• Thin scattered trees on the approach side of the structure to increase open space between them and the building.\n• Remove or cut back shrubs along the driveway that crowd the travel lane or reduce visibility.\n• Trim overhanging tree branches along the driveway to keep the full width and height of the lane clear for vehicle access.\n• Keep the area immediately surrounding the structure as clear of shrubs and tall grass as possible given the vegetation currently wrapping around it.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is visible to approaching vehicles, given the single long access route.\n• Remove dead material from shrubs and grasses near the structure before dry season."
